                        "glosses": [
                            "Originally, the regions of India outside the three East India Company capitals of Bombay, Calcutta and Madras; hence, parts of a country outside an urban centre; the regions, rural areas."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "India",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f5bbc33-d70a-498a-8e66-b496cce85358",
                                "sense_id": "f3c1cc2e-dd96-3b0c-9ce9-b2847e493198",
                                "text": "Such are the means by which the Mofussil, “up-country,” or provincial Anglo-Indian will reach his station or district, and unless he is going to Bombay or Calcutta, which are practically the two entrance doors of the Empire, with Madras for a back door, his first experience of Anglo-Indian life will be of travel; and the land journey will often prove much more trying than the sea-voyage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3072722-130b-454e-9012-516a4e665bc1",
                                "sense_id": "f3c1cc2e-dd96-3b0c-9ce9-b2847e493198",
                                "text": "His natural language was crass and of the mofussil, yet he could pepper it with smart turns of phrase on occasion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
